\b\fs30 4. Market map: where SehatSaathi sits in India\b0\fs24\par
\par
India already has strong players in adjacent categories.\par
\par
\b\fs26 4.1 Diagnostic and consumer health players\b0\fs24\par
\par
Large adjacent brands include:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab Tata 1mg\par
\tab\bullet\tab Practo\par
\tab\bullet\tab Dr Lal PathLabs\par
\tab\bullet\tab Metropolis Healthcare\par
\tab\bullet\tab Thyrocare\par
\tab\bullet\tab Redcliffe Labs\par
\tab\bullet\tab Orange Health Labs\par
\tab\bullet\tab Healthians\par
\par
These are not all the same type of company. That distinction matters.\par
\par
\b\fs26 4.2 What these companies are actually optimized for\b0\fs24\par
\par
#### Tata 1mg\par
\par
Tata 1mg is a broad healthcare commerce platform spanning medicines, diagnostics, and doctor consultations. Its diagnostics surface emphasizes test booking, lab comparison, home collection, and specialist access. The platform claims very large consumer reach and national order volume. That makes it powerful on convenience, distribution, and transaction aggregation, but not necessarily focused on deep continuity between reports and follow-up planning.\par
\par
#### Practo\par
\par
Practo is stronger in doctor discovery, appointment booking, teleconsultation, and practice-management tooling. Practo Ray already serves operational workflows for clinics and has explicit ABDM positioning. That makes Practo a relevant comparison not because it is doing the same product today, but because it already owns part of the provider workflow surface that SehatSaathi may want to enter.\par
\par
#### Dr Lal PathLabs, Metropolis, Thyrocare\par
\par
These are major diagnostics businesses with brand trust, scale, and distribution. Their core advantage is not fancy patient UX. It is network scale, test volume, quality process, established collection and processing infrastructure, and high trust in results. A startup should not assume it can out-distribute them. But it may help them, or smaller competitors, create a better continuity layer on top of the report.\par
\par
#### Redcliffe, Orange Health, Healthians\par
\par
These players sit closer to digitally enabled diagnostics and home collection behavior. They are relevant because they show where the market is moving: convenience, turnaround time, app-layer experience, and user retention. They also prove that diagnostics players are willing to invest in digital engagement if it affects booking, repeat, and trust.\par
\par
\b\fs26 4.3 SehatSaathi’s potential category\b0\fs24\par
\par
SehatSaathi is not strongest when compared as “another app where people upload reports.”\par
\par
It is strongest when positioned as:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab continuity software for diagnostics and outpatient follow-up\par
\tab\bullet\tab an intelligence layer between report delivery and next clinical action\par
\tab\bullet\tab a follow-up infrastructure layer that can sit inside lab, clinic, or hospital workflow\par
\par
That category is less crowded than consumer diagnostics booking.\par
