\b\fs30 8. Legal and compliance working model for India\b0\fs24\par
\par
This is not formal legal advice. It is a founder operating framework based on current official policy and regulatory context.\par
\par
\b\fs26 8.1 What legal bucket SehatSaathi is currently closest to\b0\fs24\par
\par
Right now SehatSaathi is best treated as:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab a digital health software layer\par
\tab\bullet\tab a health-data processing product\par
\tab\bullet\tab a continuity and follow-up support system\par
\par
It should avoid behaving like:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab a diagnostic decision-maker\par
\tab\bullet\tab a registered medical practitioner substitute\par
\tab\bullet\tab a telemedicine platform making clinical decisions on its own\par
\par
\b\fs26 8.2 DPDP Act implications\b0\fs24\par
\par
The Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 matters because SehatSaathi processes sensitive health-linked personal data in digital form. That means your company will function as a data fiduciary for at least some flows, and potentially a data processor in certain white-label or partner arrangements depending on contract structure.\par
\par
Practical implications:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab explicit and intelligible consent matters\par
\tab\bullet\tab purpose limitation matters\par
\tab\bullet\tab retention limitation matters\par
\tab\bullet\tab deletion and export rights matter\par
\tab\bullet\tab child data handling matters\par
\tab\bullet\tab access control matters\par
\par
What this means operationally:\par
\par
\b 1.\b0 You need a very clear patient consent surface before report analysis and data linking.\par
\b 2.\b0 You should minimize unnecessary profile collection.\par
\b 3.\b0 You should maintain delete and export controls visibly.\par
\b 4.\b0 If working with minors, parent/guardian logic becomes important.\par
\b 5.\b0 Partner contracts must clearly define who is controller-like and who is processor-like in each workflow.\par
\par
\b\fs26 8.3 ABDM / ABHA implications\b0\fs24\par
\par
ABDM is strategically important because it offers a national digital health architecture and a trust language that Indian institutions already understand.\par
\par
But ABHA linkage also increases sensitivity. If you integrate deeper into ABDM or ABHA-linked flows, then consent, data handling, and interoperability expectations become more serious.\par
\par
Good news:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab ABDM is aligned with digital health continuity\par
\tab\bullet\tab HFR/HPR/PHR positioning can support ecosystem credibility\par
\par
Risk:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab if you market sloppy AI report advice while sitting near ABHA-linked identity or records, trust damage becomes worse\par
\par
Recommendation:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab use ABDM alignment as a workflow credibility layer\par
\tab\bullet\tab do not overclaim official authority\par
\tab\bullet\tab keep user control and consent explicit\par
\par
\b\fs26 8.4 Telemedicine implications\b0\fs24\par
\par
India’s telemedicine guidelines are built around the Registered Medical Practitioner. This matters because software can support telemedicine, but should not casually pretend to become the practitioner.\par
\par
For SehatSaathi:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab report guidance should remain non-diagnostic\par
\tab\bullet\tab doctor questions are good\par
\tab\bullet\tab doctor handoff is good\par
\tab\bullet\tab triage organization is okay\par
\tab\bullet\tab clinical instruction or prescription logic without a doctor is risky\par
\par
Therefore:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab keep patient-facing language framed as follow-up support\par
\tab\bullet\tab never imply final diagnosis from report alone\par
\tab\bullet\tab if teleconsult is added, ensure the doctor role remains explicit and compliant\par
\par
\b\fs26 8.5 Clinical establishment and partner implications\b0\fs24\par
\par
If partnering with labs and hospitals, two realities matter:\par
\par
\b 1.\b0 Compliance expectations become more enterprise-like even if no one asks for them on day one.\par
\b 2.\b0 Institutional buyers care about data separation, audit trails, and access control.\par
\par
That means your product roadmap should include:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab role-based access\par
\tab\bullet\tab upload audit trails\par
\tab\bullet\tab patient ownership boundaries\par
\tab\bullet\tab partner-specific data views\par
\tab\bullet\tab vendor agreements and DPAs\par
\par
\b\fs26 8.6 Legal operating recommendation\b0\fs24\par
\par
Short version:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab stay out of diagnosis language\par
\tab\bullet\tab stay inside follow-up support language\par
\tab\bullet\tab use explicit consent\par
\tab\bullet\tab build deletion/export/retention cleanly\par
\tab\bullet\tab prepare partner contracts carefully\par
\tab\bullet\tab if you go deeper into ABHA and clinical workflows, get proper legal review before scale\par
\par
