\b\fs30 10. Pricing strategy recommendation\b0\fs24\par
\par
\b\fs26 10.1 Do not price too cheaply just because India is price-sensitive\b0\fs24\par
\par
If you price too low, two bad things happen:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab buyers think it is non-essential\par
\tab\bullet\tab you do not have room for support, onboarding, and compliance cost\par
\par
\b\fs26 10.2 Suggested pricing frames\b0\fs24\par
\par
#### Independent labs / small chains\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab monthly branch license: INR 7,500 to INR 20,000\par
\tab\bullet\tab or usage model: INR 8 to INR 25 per analyzed report\par
\par
#### Clinics\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab per doctor or per clinic subscription: INR 4,000 to INR 15,000 per month\par
\par
#### Hospitals / larger groups\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab annual contract with setup + usage or location pricing\par
\par
\b\fs26 10.3 Best early commercial structure\b0\fs24\par
\par
For early pilots:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab no large setup fee\par
\tab\bullet\tab pilot fee or subsidized paid pilot\par
\tab\bullet\tab clear success metrics\par
\tab\bullet\tab defined conversion path after pilot\par
\par
You should avoid free pilots that have no decision deadline.\par
\par
\par_______________________________________________________________\par
\par
\b\fs30 11. Cost structure: what this product really costs\b0\fs24\par
\par
Below is the practical cost stack for SehatSaathi.\par
\par
\b\fs26 11.1 Product architecture reality\b0\fs24\par
\par
Important product reality from the current codebase:\par
\par
Today, SehatSaathi’s report-summary and action-plan path is not heavily dependent on OpenAI per report. The current flow is primarily:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab report upload\par
\tab\bullet\tab OCR / extraction\par
\tab\bullet\tab deterministic parsing\par
\tab\bullet\tab deterministic guided follow-up intelligence\par
\tab\bullet\tab deterministic plan generation\par
\par
That is good news because it means your current variable cost per report is driven more by OCR/extraction and infrastructure than by LLM cost.\par
\par
This materially improves margin potential.\par
\par
\b\fs26 11.2 Core cost buckets\b0\fs24\par
\par
#### A. Infrastructure\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab app hosting\par
\tab\bullet\tab API hosting\par
\tab\bullet\tab database\par
\tab\bullet\tab file storage\par
\tab\bullet\tab logging/monitoring\par
\tab\bullet\tab backups\par
\par
#### B. Document extraction\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab Azure Document Intelligence or equivalent OCR layer\par
\par
#### C. Optional AI layer\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab OpenAI for future enhancement, triage, doctor assist, or premium generation features\par
\par
#### D. Communication\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab OTP / SMS\par
\tab\bullet\tab WhatsApp\par
\tab\bullet\tab email\par
\par
#### E. Team\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab founder draw\par
\tab\bullet\tab engineer(s)\par
\tab\bullet\tab ops / support\par
\tab\bullet\tab sales / field BD\par
\par
#### F. Compliance / admin\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab legal contracts\par
\tab\bullet\tab GST / accounting\par
\tab\bullet\tab privacy policy / DPA work\par
\par
#### G. Sales and marketing\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab field demos\par
\tab\bullet\tab travel\par
\tab\bullet\tab partner materials\par
\tab\bullet\tab light digital marketing\par
\par
