\b\fs30 27. Detailed go-to-market model\b0\fs24\par
\par
\b\fs26 27.1 Recommended GTM sequence\b0\fs24\par
\par
#### Step 1: founder-led sales\par
\par
At this stage, no one can sell the product better than the founder, because the product category is still being defined.\par
\par
You should personally handle:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab demos\par
\tab\bullet\tab objection handling\par
\tab\bullet\tab pilot setup\par
\tab\bullet\tab weekly review loops\par
\tab\bullet\tab partner feedback\par
\par
#### Step 2: paid or semi-paid pilot\par
\par
Free pilots create polite interest.\par
\par
Paid pilots create seriousness.\par
\par
Even INR 5,000 to INR 15,000 per month matters because it reveals whether the partner sees real value.\par
\par
#### Step 3: measurable outcomes\par
\par
Choose a small set of metrics:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab report open rate\par
\tab\bullet\tab follow-up plan interaction rate\par
\tab\bullet\tab repeat upload or repeat report continuity\par
\tab\bullet\tab doctor question usage\par
\tab\bullet\tab repeat testing retention\par
\par
Without metrics, your product stays “nice.”\par
\par
#### Step 4: repeatable deployment kit\par
\par
Every new partner should receive:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab a simple setup checklist\par
\tab\bullet\tab front-desk script\par
\tab\bullet\tab patient-facing poster\par
\tab\bullet\tab escalation/support flow\par
\tab\bullet\tab privacy explanation\par
\tab\bullet\tab sample success screenshots\par
\par
#### Step 5: narrow specialization if needed\par
\par
If one segment responds much better than others, go narrower before going broader.\par
\par
Example:\par
\par
If diabetes clinics or endocrine-linked labs respond strongly, build there first. Narrowness often beats horizontal storytelling.\par
\par
\b\fs26 27.2 Sales motion economics\b0\fs24\par
\par
Here is the founder trap to avoid:\par
\par
If it takes 20 meetings and 6 weeks to close a partner worth INR 8,000 a month, the sales model is weak unless that partner expands into multi-branch volume.\par
\par
So you need to know quickly:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab how many meetings per close\par
\tab\bullet\tab how long to close\par
\tab\bullet\tab who signs\par
\tab\bullet\tab what the real annual value is\par
\par
#### Healthy early sales pattern\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab 3 to 6 relevant meetings\par
\tab\bullet\tab 2 to 4 weeks to pilot\par
\tab\bullet\tab 4 to 8 weeks to paid continuation\par
\par
#### Unhealthy early sales pattern\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab endless enthusiasm\par
\tab\bullet\tab no usage\par
\tab\bullet\tab no commitment\par
\tab\bullet\tab no budget owner\par
\par
\b\fs26 27.3 Founder sales scripts\b0\fs24\par
\par
#### For labs\par
\par
“Today, most labs send a report and lose continuity. We help you convert that result into a calmer follow-up experience that improves patient trust and keeps the next step organized.”\par
\par
#### For clinics\par
\par
“Patients come back with scattered reports and confusion. We prepare the patient better before the next review, without replacing the doctor.”\par
\par
#### For hospitals\par
\par
“This is a continuity and follow-up layer that reduces noise between diagnostics, patient understanding, and clinician review.”\par
\par
