\b\fs30 28. Legal working checklist before meaningful scale\b0\fs24\par
\par
Below is the practical founder checklist, not legal theatre.\par
\par
\b\fs26 28.1 Patient consent\b0\fs24\par
\par
You should have:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab clear report analysis consent\par
\tab\bullet\tab clear storage and use disclosure\par
\tab\bullet\tab clear partner-linked consent where relevant\par
\tab\bullet\tab clear ability to withdraw or delete\par
\par
\b\fs26 28.2 Role clarity\b0\fs24\par
\par
You need contract and product clarity on:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab who is the primary user\par
\tab\bullet\tab whether the lab is only uploading or also distributing the continuity layer\par
\tab\bullet\tab whether SehatSaathi is independent or white-labeled\par
\tab\bullet\tab who responds to user complaints\par
\par
\b\fs26 28.3 Data retention\b0\fs24\par
\par
Define:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab how long uploaded reports are retained\par
\tab\bullet\tab what happens after deletion requests\par
\tab\bullet\tab how backups are handled\par
\tab\bullet\tab how partner separation works\par
\par
\b\fs26 28.4 Security expectations\b0\fs24\par
\par
Before scale, you should at least be able to defend:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab access control\par
\tab\bullet\tab audit logs\par
\tab\bullet\tab upload-source trails\par
\tab\bullet\tab account-based ownership\par
\tab\bullet\tab deletion/export functioning\par
\par
\b\fs26 28.5 Sensitive messaging\b0\fs24\par
\par
Your product copy should avoid:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab disease naming from isolated reports\par
\tab\bullet\tab emergency escalation unless truly justified\par
\tab\bullet\tab pseudo-prescription language\par
\tab\bullet\tab casual medical certainty\par
\par
\b\fs26 28.6 Pediatric and special populations\b0\fs24\par
\par
Because the system now uses age and sex context, be careful:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab pediatric interpretation should remain cautious\par
\tab\bullet\tab pregnancy-related implications should be handled carefully if ever added\par
\tab\bullet\tab family-linked records must keep consent and identity boundaries clean\par
\par
\b\fs26 28.7 Formal legal work you should actually budget for\b0\fs24\par
\par
At some point before wider scale, spend for:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab terms of use review\par
\tab\bullet\tab privacy policy review\par
\tab\bullet\tab partner DPA/vendor agreement templates\par
\tab\bullet\tab pilot agreement template\par
\tab\bullet\tab white-label contract template\par
\tab\bullet\tab clinical disclaimer review\par
\par
This is not optional forever.\par
