\b\fs30 30. Profitability sensitivity analysis\b0\fs24\par
\par
This section answers the question: what really changes whether you make money?\par
\par
\b\fs26 30.1 Sensitivity factor 1: acquisition model\b0\fs24\par
\par
If acquisition is:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab partner-distributed: business can work\par
\tab\bullet\tab paid D2C: business is much weaker\par
\par
This is the single biggest lever.\par
\par
\b\fs26 30.2 Sensitivity factor 2: price realization\b0\fs24\par
\par
If your average partner value is:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab INR 5,000/month: hard\par
\tab\bullet\tab INR 10,000 to INR 15,000/month: workable\par
\tab\bullet\tab INR 20,000+/month or multi-branch equivalent: attractive\par
\par
\b\fs26 30.3 Sensitivity factor 3: report volume vs support load\b0\fs24\par
\par
High report volume is not enough if:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab support load is high\par
\tab\bullet\tab extraction failures are high\par
\tab\bullet\tab partner staff need handholding\par
\par
You want clean volume, not messy volume.\par
\par
\b\fs26 30.4 Sensitivity factor 4: clinical restraint\b0\fs24\par
\par
Overconfident output may superficially increase engagement in the short term, but it destroys trust in the medium term.\par
\par
In healthcare, responsible restraint is not just ethics. It is business durability.\par
\par
\b\fs26 30.5 Sensitivity factor 5: repeat use\b0\fs24\par
\par
If the product creates:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab repeated plan opens\par
\tab\bullet\tab repeated follow-up review\par
\tab\bullet\tab repeated report continuity\par
\par
then partner ROI strengthens.\par
\par
If it is only a one-time curiosity layer, pricing power weakens.\par
\par
\b\fs26 30.6 Simple break-even math\b0\fs24\par
\par
Using a mid-stage monthly operating cost of INR 6.2 lakh:\par
\par
#### At INR 10,000 monthly average partner value\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab break-even partners needed: about 62\par
\par
#### At INR 15,000 monthly average partner value\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab break-even partners needed: about 42\par
\par
#### At INR 20,000 monthly average partner value\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab break-even partners needed: about 31\par
\par
That is a much more promising picture than consumer break-even math.\par
\par
\b\fs26 30.7 Founder take-home potential\b0\fs24\par
\par
If the business reaches:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab 100 partner locations\par
\tab\bullet\tab average realized value of INR 12,000/month\par
\tab\bullet\tab annualized revenue of INR 1.44 crore\par
\tab\bullet\tab annual operating cost of roughly INR 72 lakh to INR 96 lakh\par
\par
then operating surplus can be roughly:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab INR 48 lakh to INR 72 lakh before tax in a disciplined structure\par
\par
That is not unicorn math. It is real-business math.\par
\par
This is exactly why B2B2C is the right lens here.\par
