\b\fs30 34. What proof you need before calling this a company, not just a product\b0\fs24\par
\par
There are different stages of proof. Founders often confuse them.\par
\par
\b\fs26 34.1 Product proof\b0\fs24\par
\par
You mostly have this.\par
\par
Questions answered:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab Can the workflow function?\par
\tab\bullet\tab Can reports be ingested?\par
\tab\bullet\tab Can summary and plan be produced?\par
\tab\bullet\tab Can the lab side and patient side connect?\par
\par
Mostly yes.\par
\par
\b\fs26 34.2 Trust proof\b0\fs24\par
\par
You are partway there.\par
\par
Questions:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab Do users feel calmer rather than more anxious?\par
\tab\bullet\tab Do doctors feel supported rather than replaced?\par
\tab\bullet\tab Do labs feel safer rather than exposed?\par
\par
This needs real-world validation, not only internal conviction.\par
\par
\b\fs26 34.3 Commercial proof\b0\fs24\par
\par
This is not proven until:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab someone pays\par
\tab\bullet\tab someone renews\par
\tab\bullet\tab someone expands usage\par
\par
Pilot praise is not proof.\par
\par
Renewal is proof.\par
\par
\b\fs26 34.4 Outcome proof\b0\fs24\par
\par
This matters if you want real pricing power.\par
\par
Can you show:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab more repeat follow-up\par
\tab\bullet\tab better patient readiness\par
\tab\bullet\tab more report engagement\par
\tab\bullet\tab more repeat retention for partner\par
\par
Even directional evidence helps.\par
\par
\b\fs26 34.5 Scale proof\b0\fs24\par
\par
This is later and should not be faked.\par
\par
Scale proof means:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab many report styles\par
\tab\bullet\tab many users\par
\tab\bullet\tab many partners\par
\tab\bullet\tab manageable support burden\par
\tab\bullet\tab healthy gross margin\par
\par
Do not jump mentally from working product to proven company. Those are different milestones.\par
\par
