\b\fs30 36. Three-year scenario view\b0\fs24\par
\par
This section is not a forecast. It is a strategic map of what the business could become under different execution choices.\par
\par
\b\fs26 36.1 Scenario A: disciplined B2B2C success\b0\fs24\par
\par
#### Year 1\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab 10 to 25 partner locations\par
\tab\bullet\tab paid pilots and early renewals\par
\tab\bullet\tab strong lab/clinic wedge\par
\tab\bullet\tab founder still deeply involved\par
\par
#### Year 2\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab 50 to 150 partner locations\par
\tab\bullet\tab clearer repeatable onboarding\par
\tab\bullet\tab better partner analytics\par
\tab\bullet\tab early white-label conversations\par
\par
#### Year 3\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab regional brand inside diagnostics continuity\par
\tab\bullet\tab meaningful recurring revenue\par
\tab\bullet\tab stronger team\par
\tab\bullet\tab optional expansion to more clinical pathways\par
\par
This is the healthiest path.\par
\par
\b\fs26 36.2 Scenario B: D2C distraction\b0\fs24\par
\par
#### Year 1\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab consumer downloads\par
\tab\bullet\tab scattered uploads\par
\tab\bullet\tab weak retention\par
\tab\bullet\tab ad spend begins\par
\par
#### Year 2\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab product gets pulled toward generic health content, reminders, and acquisition hacks\par
\tab\bullet\tab weak revenue quality\par
\tab\bullet\tab trust messaging becomes harder to sustain\par
\par
#### Year 3\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab burn without strong moat\par
\tab\bullet\tab dependence on cross-sell or marketplace monetization\par
\par
This is the path I would caution you against.\par
\par
\b\fs26 36.3 Scenario C: enterprise-heavy too early\b0\fs24\par
\par
#### Year 1\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab long hospital conversations\par
\tab\bullet\tab heavy customization requests\par
\tab\bullet\tab little actual usage\par
\par
#### Year 2\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab product roadmap bends to enterprise edge cases before the core wedge is proven\par
\par
#### Year 3\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab fragile services business with too much complexity\par
\par
This can happen if you chase prestige logos too early.\par
\par
\b\fs26 36.4 Best strategic principle for the next three years\b0\fs24\par
\par
Stay close to the report moment, the follow-up moment, and the continuity moment.\par
\par
Do not drift into:\par
\par
\tab\bullet\tab generic wellness\par
\tab\bullet\tab diagnosis inflation\par
\tab\bullet\tab marketplace clutter\par
\tab\bullet\tab enterprise over-customization\par
\par
If you keep the product’s center of gravity clear, the company has a better chance of staying coherent.\par
